-- 신희종 교수 회신 반영 (2026-11-12, 워드 파일). 받은 항목만 바꾸고 나머지 칸은 그대로 둔다. 여러 번 실행해도 결과가 같다.
-- office(건물·호실 문구)는 building/room 기준으로 다시 만든다. 사진은 관리자 화면에서 올린다.

update faculty set
  bio_ko = $q$<h3>학력</h3><ul><li>서울대학교 화학생물공학부 2014 공학사</li><li>서울대학교 화학생물공학부 2020 공학박사</li></ul><h3>경력</h3><ul><li>기초과학연구원(IBS) 나노입자 연구단 박사후연구원 (2020–2022)</li><li>Northwestern University 화학과 박사후연구원 (2023–2025)</li><li>서강대학교 화공생명공학과 조교수 (2025–현재)</li></ul><h3>주요 수상</h3><ul><li>한국공업화학회 미원상사신진과학자상 (2026)</li><li>한국연구재단 세종과학펠로우십 국외연수 트랙 선정 (2023–2025)</li><li>동진쎄미켐 동진과학기술상 최우수연구상 (2021)</li></ul><h3>주요 논문</h3><ul><li>"Regulation of proton transference for stable and efficient reactive capture of CO₂ from air," <em>Nature Energy</em> (2026)</li><li>"Gold-Stabilized Copper Enables Anodic Hydrogen Evolution for Ultralow-Voltage CO-to-Ethylene Electrolysis," <em>Advanced Materials</em> 38, e74459 (2026) <a href="https://doi.org/10.1002/adma.74459">doi.org/10.1002/adma.74459</a></li><li>"Tandem amine scrubbing and CO₂ electrolysis via direct piperazine carbamate reduction," <em>Nature Energy</em> 10, 1262–1273 (2025) <a href="https://doi.org/10.1038/s41560-025-01869-8">doi.org/10.1038/s41560-025-01869-8</a></li><li>"Electrolysis of ethylene to ethylene glycol paired with acidic CO₂-to-CO conversion," <em>Energy &amp; Environmental Science</em> 18, 8600–8607 (2025) <a href="https://doi.org/10.1039/D5EE02847G">doi.org/10.1039/D5EE02847G</a></li><li>"Hierarchically porous carbon supports enable efficient syngas production in electrified reactive capture," <em>Energy &amp; Environmental Science</em> 18, 6628–6640 (2025) <a href="https://doi.org/10.1039/D5EE00094G">doi.org/10.1039/D5EE00094G</a></li><li>"Efficient H₂O₂ Electrosynthesis in Acidic Media via Multiscale Catalyst Optimization," <em>Advanced Materials</em> 37, e2418489 (2025) <a href="https://doi.org/10.1002/adma.202418489">doi.org/10.1002/adma.202418489</a></li><li>"Electrochemically generated electrophilic peroxo species accelerates alkaline oxygen evolution reaction," <em>Joule</em> 7, 1902–1919 (2023) <a href="https://doi.org/10.1016/j.joule.2023.06.018">doi.org/10.1016/j.joule.2023.06.018</a></li><li>"Supramolecular tuning of supported metal phthalocyanine catalysts for hydrogen peroxide electrosynthesis," <em>Nature Catalysis</em> 6, 234–243 (2023) <a href="https://doi.org/10.1038/s41929-023-00924-5">doi.org/10.1038/s41929-023-00924-5</a></li><li>"Atomic-level tuning of Co–N–C catalyst for high-performance electrochemical H₂O₂ production," <em>Nature Materials</em> 19, 436–442 (2020) <a href="https://doi.org/10.1038/s41563-019-0571-5">doi.org/10.1038/s41563-019-0571-5</a></li></ul>$q$,
  bio_en = $q$<h3>Education</h3><ul><li>B.S., School of Chemical and Biological Engineering, Seoul National University (2014)</li><li>Ph.D., School of Chemical and Biological Engineering, Seoul National University (2020)</li></ul><h3>Experience</h3><ul><li>Postdoctoral Researcher, Center for Nanoparticle Research, Institute for Basic Science (IBS) (2020–2022)</li><li>Postdoctoral Researcher, Department of Chemistry, Northwestern University (2023–2025)</li><li>Assistant Professor, Department of Chemical and Biomolecular Engineering, Sogang University (2025–present)</li></ul><h3>Selected Awards</h3><ul><li>Miwon Commercial Young Scientist Award, Korean Society of Industrial and Engineering Chemistry (2026)</li><li>Sejong Science Fellowship (Overseas Training Track), National Research Foundation of Korea (2023–2025)</li><li>Dongjin Science and Technology Award – Best Research Award, Dongjin Semichem (2021)</li></ul><h3>Selected Publications</h3><ul><li>"Regulation of proton transference for stable and efficient reactive capture of CO₂ from air," <em>Nature Energy</em> (2026)</li><li>"Gold-Stabilized Copper Enables Anodic Hydrogen Evolution for Ultralow-Voltage CO-to-Ethylene Electrolysis," <em>Advanced Materials</em> 38, e74459 (2026) <a href="https://doi.org/10.1002/adma.74459">doi.org/10.1002/adma.74459</a></li><li>"Tandem amine scrubbing and CO₂ electrolysis via direct piperazine carbamate reduction," <em>Nature Energy</em> 10, 1262–1273 (2025) <a href="https://doi.org/10.1038/s41560-025-01869-8">doi.org/10.1038/s41560-025-01869-8</a></li><li>"Electrolysis of ethylene to ethylene glycol paired with acidic CO₂-to-CO conversion," <em>Energy &amp; Environmental Science</em> 18, 8600–8607 (2025) <a href="https://doi.org/10.1039/D5EE02847G">doi.org/10.1039/D5EE02847G</a></li><li>"Hierarchically porous carbon supports enable efficient syngas production in electrified reactive capture," <em>Energy &amp; Environmental Science</em> 18, 6628–6640 (2025) <a href="https://doi.org/10.1039/D5EE00094G">doi.org/10.1039/D5EE00094G</a></li><li>"Efficient H₂O₂ Electrosynthesis in Acidic Media via Multiscale Catalyst Optimization," <em>Advanced Materials</em> 37, e2418489 (2025) <a href="https://doi.org/10.1002/adma.202418489">doi.org/10.1002/adma.202418489</a></li><li>"Electrochemically generated electrophilic peroxo species accelerates alkaline oxygen evolution reaction," <em>Joule</em> 7, 1902–1919 (2023) <a href="https://doi.org/10.1016/j.joule.2023.06.018">doi.org/10.1016/j.joule.2023.06.018</a></li><li>"Supramolecular tuning of supported metal phthalocyanine catalysts for hydrogen peroxide electrosynthesis," <em>Nature Catalysis</em> 6, 234–243 (2023) <a href="https://doi.org/10.1038/s41929-023-00924-5">doi.org/10.1038/s41929-023-00924-5</a></li><li>"Atomic-level tuning of Co–N–C catalyst for high-performance electrochemical H₂O₂ production," <em>Nature Materials</em> 19, 436–442 (2020) <a href="https://doi.org/10.1038/s41563-019-0571-5">doi.org/10.1038/s41563-019-0571-5</a></li></ul>$q$,
  research_ko = $q$<p>전기화학 에너지 변환 연구실(EECL)은 지속가능한 에너지 및 화학산업을 위한 고효율 전기촉매 소재와 전기화학 시스템을 연구합니다. 전극–전해질 계면에서 발생하는 물리화학적 상호작용과 반응 메커니즘을 이해하고, 이를 기반으로 전기화학 반응의 활성, 선택성 및 안정성을 향상시키는 연구를 수행합니다. 특히 X선 기반 분광법 및 질량분석법 등 다양한 실시간 분석 기술을 활용하여 촉매의 동적 구조 변화와 반응 경로를 규명합니다. 이러한 기초적 이해를 실제 전해조 시스템의 설계와 최적화에 적용하여 기존 화학공정의 전기화(Electrification)와 탄소중립형 화학물질 생산 기술을 개발하고자 합니다.</p><p>전기촉매 및 전극–전해질 계면 공학<br>전기촉매의 활성, 선택성 및 안정성을 결정하는 전극–전해질 계면의 물리화학적 상호작용을 연구합니다. 금속 및 금속산화물, 단원자 및 분자 촉매 등 다양한 소재를 대상으로 실시간 분광학적 분석(In situ/Operando Spectroscopy)을 통해 촉매의 산화상태, 표면 재구성 및 반응 중간체의 변화를 규명하고, 이를 기반으로 고효율·고안정성 전기촉매와 계면 설계 전략을 개발합니다.</p><p>이산화탄소 포집 및 전기화학적 전환<br>대기 및 산업 배출원 등 다양한 CO₂ 공급원을 대상으로 포집과 전기화학적 전환을 통합하여 에너지 소비를 줄이고 탄소 이용 효율을 높이는 기술을 연구합니다. 특히 탄산염, 중탄산염 및 아민계 포집 용액에서 CO₂를 직접 유용한 화학 원료로 전환하는 촉매와 반응 시스템을 개발합니다. 또한 막전극접합체(MEA) 및 전해조 구조 최적화를 통해 고효율 통합 CO₂ 포집·전환 공정의 구현을 목표로 합니다.</p><p>고효율 수전해 및 수소 생산<br>재생에너지 기반 그린수소 생산을 위한 고효율·고안정성 수전해 촉매 소재 및 전극 시스템을 개발합니다. 특히 산소발생반응(OER)에서 촉매의 전자구조, 산화·환원 거동 및 계면 화학을 제어하여 반응 활성과 내구성을 향상시키고, 다양한 전해질 환경에서 안정적으로 작동하는 수전해 기술을 연구합니다.</p><p>고부가가치 화학물질의 선택적 전기화학 합성 및 자원순환<br>재생전력을 활용하여 과산화수소(H₂O₂)와 고부가가치 화학물질을 선택적으로 생산하는 전기화학 기술을 연구합니다. 산소의 2전자 환원반응을 통한 과산화수소 합성과 유기화합물 및 폐플라스틱 유래 원료의 선택적 전기산화 기술을 개발하며, 양극과 음극의 유용한 반응을 결합하는 짝전기분해(Paired Electrolysis)를 통해 에너지 효율적이고 지속가능한 화학물질 생산 공정을 구현하고자 합니다.</p>$q$,
  research_en = $q$<p>The Electrochemical Energy Conversion Laboratory (EECL) develops high-efficiency electrocatalytic materials and electrochemical systems for sustainable energy and chemical industries. We seek to understand the physicochemical interactions and reaction mechanisms at the electrode–electrolyte interface, and use that understanding to improve the activity, selectivity, and stability of electrochemical reactions. Using a range of real-time techniques, including X-ray spectroscopy and mass spectrometry, we track the dynamic structural changes of catalysts and identify reaction pathways. We then carry this fundamental insight into the design and optimization of practical electrolyzers, with the goal of electrifying conventional chemical processes and producing chemicals in a carbon-neutral way.</p><p>Electrocatalysis and Electrode–Electrolyte Interface Engineering<br>We study the physicochemical interactions at the electrode–electrolyte interface that govern the activity, selectivity, and stability of electrocatalysts. Across metals and metal oxides, single-atom catalysts, and molecular catalysts, we use in situ/operando spectroscopy to follow changes in oxidation state, surface reconstruction, and reaction intermediates, and from this develop highly active, durable electrocatalysts and interface-design strategies.</p><p>CO₂ Capture and Electrochemical Conversion<br>We integrate CO₂ capture with electrochemical conversion, for sources ranging from air to industrial emissions, to cut energy consumption and raise carbon-utilization efficiency. In particular, we develop catalysts and reaction systems that convert CO₂ directly from carbonate, bicarbonate, and amine capture solutions into valuable chemical feedstocks. Through optimization of membrane electrode assemblies (MEAs) and electrolyzer architecture, we aim to realize efficient integrated CO₂ capture-and-conversion processes.</p><p>High-Efficiency Water Electrolysis and Hydrogen Production<br>We develop efficient, durable catalyst materials and electrode systems for green hydrogen production from renewable energy. Focusing on the oxygen evolution reaction (OER), we control the electronic structure, redox behavior, and interfacial chemistry of catalysts to raise activity and durability, and study electrolysis technologies that operate stably across a range of electrolyte environments.</p><p>Selective Electrosynthesis of Value-Added Chemicals and Resource Circularity<br>We develop electrochemical technologies that use renewable electricity to selectively produce hydrogen peroxide (H₂O₂) and other value-added chemicals. These include H₂O₂ synthesis via the two-electron oxygen reduction reaction and the selective electro-oxidation of organic compounds and feedstocks derived from waste plastics. By pairing useful reactions at the anode and cathode (paired electrolysis), we aim to build energy-efficient, sustainable routes to chemical production.</p>$q$,
  lab_ko = $q$전기화학 에너지 변환 연구실$q$,
  lab_en = $q$Electrochemical Energy Conversion Laboratory (EECL)$q$,
  lab_url = $q$https://hshin-lab.com$q$,
  building = $q$R$q$,
  room = $q$603$q$,
  tel = $q$02-705-8921$q$,
  keywords = $q$Electrocatalysis & Interface Engineering, CO₂ Capture & Conversion, Water Electrolysis & Green Hydrogen, Electrochemical Synthesis of Chemicals$q$,
  office = $q$리치과학관(R) 603호$q$
where name_ko = '신희종';

select name_ko, lab_ko, lab_en, lab_url, office, room, tel, keywords, length(bio_ko) bio_ko, length(bio_en) bio_en, length(research_ko) res_ko, length(research_en) res_en from faculty where name_ko = '신희종';
